  "designBoundaries": [
    "Planning and quick discovery retain separate bounded context. Switching tools preserves page state; it does not merge their conversation histories or persist them in the database.",
    "Both tools remain mounted under native hidden containers; one request composer is visible. In-flight answers or cart saves lock cross-tool controls. Focus changes respect reduced motion and an inert page behind an item dialog.",
    "The map shortcut only selects and focuses the existing quick-question input. The Neighborhood Connection item shortcut still explicitly asks about that item.",
    "Show on map resolves a plan item through the loaded scoped catalog before highlighting vendor IDs. A prior runner highlight is cleared; a returned runner name is never treated as a runner identity or assignment.",
    "Read-only production UI verification intentionally disabled WebGL and did not invoke a model, prepare or pay for an order. Actual model and Sandbox capture evidence remains in its original reports."
  ],
